  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Satellite-Tracked Drifter Trajectories in the Bering Sea",
  "description": "Satellite-tracked drift buoys (~100) deployed in the Bering Sea. Most bouys report latitude and longitude (i..e., bouy trajectories describing ocean currents). A few drifters report sea temperature and ocean color. Drogue depth 25 - 45 m.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Explore / measure advection.",
